  "verbalization": "Myxotyroside B appears to have a direct target relationship with SF-188 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Myxotyroside B acts as a ligand that binds to VMRC-LCP, which in turn is targeted by Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, and finally, this enzyme targets SF-188. Similarly, Myxotyroside B also targets Hepatocyte, which is targeted by a related compound, and this compound also targets SF-188. These findings indicate a potential pathway where Myxotyroside B may influence SF-188 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving enzymatic activity or receptor binding. The consistent presence of these intermediates suggests a possible mechanism of action that involves the modulation of a common target, likely through a shared biochemical pathway. The evidence supports a relationship between Myxotyroside B and SF-188, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
